      "content": "That feeling of being a hollow shell is incredibly heavy, and it's understandable that you feel lost when you can't recognize yourself. This emptiness you're describing is a deep, profound exhaustion, and sometimes the most direct route out of that numbness is to simply stop fighting the feeling. If you can, try to focus on the immediate physical sensations—the weight of your body, the temperature of the air—just to ground yourself in the present moment.",
      "source": "target",
